        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>Anterior cervical hypertrichosis (ACH) or &apos;hairy throat&apos; refers to the presence of a tuft of terminal hair on the anterior neck, just above the laryngeal prominence.</babelon:source_value>
