        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>Cloacal exstrophy is a severe anterior abdominal wall defect in which the two hemibladders are visible and are separated by a midline intestinal plate, an omphalocele, and an imperforate anus.</babelon:source_value>
