        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>Palilalia is the involuntary repetition of one&apos;s own phrases, words, or syllables 2 or more times in a row. Typically, palilalic utterances decrease in volume with the increasing number of repetitions. Sometimes, the repetitions are also uttered with an accelerating speed.</babelon:source_value>
