        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>The presence of mildly increased concentrations of albumin in the urine, defined as an albumin-creatinine ratio (ACR) less than 30 mg/gm (less than 3.4 mg/mmol).</babelon:source_value>
