        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>Elevation of the midupper arm circumference midway between the acromion and olecranon processes of the ulna with the use of a steel or fiberglass tape. This measure is a proxy for the muscle mass of the upper arm and can be used as a part of the assessment of nutritional status in children.</babelon:source_value>
